     :capability "LINE Platform POSTs event objects (message, follow, unfollow, join, leave, postback, beacon, videoPlayComplete, unsend, activated/deactivated, memberJoined/memberLeft) to the business bot server; each event carries source.userId (format U[0-9a-f]{32}, issued per provider) for users who added the OA or chatted with the bot; also carries replyToken and message content metadata. No displayName in webhook — get it via…"
     :auth "LINE Official Account + Messaging API channel with webhook URL enabled in LINE Developers Console"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/getting-user-ids/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/receiving-messages/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/user-consent/"]}
    {:name "Messaging API — send messages (push / multicast / broadcast / narrowcast / reply)"
     :capability "Push to one user/group/room by userId; multicast to a list of userIds; broadcast to all OA friends; narrowcast by demographic attributes (age/gender/region/OS) or retargeting audiences (privacy floors: attribute targeting needs target reach ≥100, final recipient set ≥50, each audience ≥50; Thai under-20s excluded from filtered sends); reply within replyToken. Sending is the business's write surface — data flows…"
     :auth "Channel access token (Messaging API channel; broadcast/narrowcast recipients must be OA friends)"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/sending-messages/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/reference/messaging-api/#send-narrowcast-message"]}
    {:name "Messaging API — Get profile (bot friend profile)"
     :capability "GET /v2/bot/profile/{userId} returns userId, displayName, pictureUrl (https), statusMessage, language — only for users who added the OA as friend or messaged the bot and gave profile-access consent; blocked users return error; group/room members via dedicated endpoints. Bots get NO email address, NO phone number, NO birthday/gender/address via this API (those require LINE Login ID-token claims with LINE Profile+…"
     :auth "Channel access token; per-user consent on profile info"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/basics/user-profile/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/reference/messaging-api/#get-profile"]}
    {:name "Messaging API — user ID collection"
     :capability "Collect userIds from: webhook source.userId (follow/message events), GET /v2/bot/followers/ids (all friends' userIds — only for VERIFIED or PREMIUM LINE Official Accounts), group/room member ID endpoints (also verified/premium only), developer's own userId shown in the console. userId is stable per provider across that provider's Messaging API and LINE Login channels (same person links across your bot and your…"
     :auth "Messaging API channel; follower/member listing requires verified or premium OA account"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/getting-user-ids/"]}
    {:name "Messaging API — audience (retargeting) data"
     :capability "Create audiences from: uploaded userId/IFA lists (IFA/Identifier-for-Advertisers only for approved corporate applicants; JSON ≤10,000 IDs per request, file ≤1,500,000), message-click audiences (who clicked a URL), message-impression audiences (who read a message). Audiences usable for narrowcast and shareable with LINE Ads Manager via Business Manager (sharing itself needs verified/premium). Available only to OAs…"
     :auth "Channel access token on Messaging API channel; country-restricted OA; Business Manager for cross-tool sharing"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/using-audience/"]}
    {:name "Messaging API — Insight / statistics endpoints (same data shown in OA Manager)"
     :capability "Aggregated, non-personal stats readable via API: GET /v2/bot/insight/followers (friend count as of date, targetedReaches, blocks; computed ~daily, data from 2016-11-01 on), /v2/bot/insight/message/delivery (delivery counts per broadcast/targeting), /v2/bot/insight/demographic (friend demographics as 'deemed attributes' — gender/age/area/appType/subscription-period buckets, only if target reach ≥20 and OA created in…"
     :auth "Channel access token; demographic endpoint country/reach-gated"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/rate-limits/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/unit-based-statistics-aggregation/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/reference/messaging-api/#insights"]}
    {:name "LINE Login v2.1 (OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect)"
     :capability "Social login for web/iOS/Android/Unity/Flutter. Authorize at https://access.line.me/oauth2/v2.1/authorize with scopes: openid (→ ID-token sub = the provider-scoped LINE userId), profile (→ displayName, pictureUrl, statusMessage via GET /v2/profile and ID-token name/picture claims), email (→ email claim in ID token ONLY after you apply and LINE approves 'Email address permission' in the Developers console). Access…"
     :auth "LINE Login channel (provider only — no LINE Official Account required) + user consent screen; channel secret for token exchange; email scope needs LINE approval"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/line-login/integrate-line-login/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/line-login/verify-id-token/" "https://access.line.me/oauth2/v2.1/authorize"]}
    {:name "LIFF (LINE Front-end Framework)"
     :capability "Web apps inside LINE. liff.init() logs the user in; liff.getProfile() returns userId, displayName, pictureUrl, statusMessage (needs 'profile' scope selected on the LIFF app); liff.getDecodedIDToken()/getIDToken() returns OIDC claims incl. email (with approved email scope) — but NEVER POST these client-side values to your server unverified; send the ID token or access token to your server and verify via…"
     :auth "LIFF app registered under a Messaging API or LINE Login channel; user opens app inside LINE (or logs in for external browser)"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/liff/getting-started/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/liff/using-user-profile/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/reference/liff/#get-profile"]}
    {:name "LINE Official Account Manager (manager.line.me)"
     :capability "Web console for the OA itself: friend counts and follower growth, message-delivery results per broadcast, rich-menu click/impression analytics, LINE Touch (chat) analytics, friend-adding-path statistics (aggregate, no individual identity), chat transcripts with users, audience & coupon management, billing/plan changes (Communication/Light/Standard). Data viewable by console roles (Admin etc.); same underlying…"
     :auth "LINE account with role on the OA (Business ID-verified corporate identity to create the OA)"
     :urls ["https://manager.line.me/" "https://www.lycbiz.com/jp/manual/OfficialAccountManager/"]}
    {:name "LINE Ads API / Ad Tech API / Data Provider API (LINE Ads, a.k.a. LAD/ads business analytics)"
     :capability "Programmatic reporting and data for LINE advertising: LINE Ads API (campaign/delivery reports), Ad Tech API (measurement partners), Data Provider API (partner-feed 'DATA PLATFORM' integrations for advertisers & data partners). Current spec v3 (latest release 3.12.3, 2026-08-05) with partner kinds 'Data Provider (General)', 'Ad Tech (General)', 'Reporting (General)'. Restricted: only corporate users who submitted…"
     :auth "LINE Ads account + corporate approval/authorization for API partner program (Business Manager org)"
     :urls ["https://ads.line.me/public-docs/data-general-partner" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/line-ads-api/about/"]}
    {:name "LINE Conversion API / LINE Tag (web & app conversion measurement)"
     :capability "Send server-side conversion events (purchases etc.) from your site/app to LINE Ads for attribution (LINE Conversion API, corporate applicants only); LINE Tag / Tracking Tag JS on owned sites builds 'Web traffic audience' retargeting pools (aggregate cookie-based, usable in OA Manager/LINE Ads — not creatable via Messaging API, only shareable)."
     :auth "LINE Ads / OA Manager account; Conversion API requires approved corporate access"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/line-conversion-api/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/using-audience/"]}
    {:name "LINE Beacon"
     :capability "BLE beacon devices linked to the OA fire webhook 'beacon' events (including enter/exit of the beacon range, with signed proximity payload) whenever a LINE user passes by — physical proximity data, tied to userId; available in Japan, Taiwan, Thailand."
     :auth "Messaging API channel + LINE-certified beacon linked to the OA; user's LINE app nearby with BT enabled"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/messaging-api/using-beacons/"]}
    {:name "Messaging API — Get content (user-sent media)"
     :capability "GET /v2/bot/message/{messageId}/content downloads image/video/audio/file content users sent to the bot (plus location text in the event itself). LINE's side: content is automatically deleted after an unspecified period from when the message was sent ('There is no guarantee for how long content is stored'), so businesses must fetch promptly if needed."
     :auth "Channel access token; message must be addressed to your bot"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/reference/messaging-api/#get-content"]}
    {:name "LINE MINI App (Common Profile Quick-fill, opt-in corporate program)"
     :capability "Application-only platform for Japan where, after in-app user consent, services can obtain Common Profile quick-fill values incl. email, name, gender, birthday, address, phone (the only sanctioned path to phone/address). Requires separate application/contract; not generally open."
     :auth "Approved LINE MINI App channel (corporate, by application) + per-user Quick-fill consent"
     :urls ["https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/basics/user-profile/" "https://developers.line.biz/en/docs/line-mini-app/"]}
 ]
 :rate-limits [
  "Send narrowcast / send broadcast / get message-delivery count / get friends count / get friend demographics / user-interaction statistics / statistics per unit / rich-menu insights (totals & by day) / test webhook endpoint: 60 requests per hour per channel — the oft-quoted 'narrowcast 5000 req/hour' is NOT the…"
  "Audience endpoints (create/add by JSON or file, click/imp audience create, rename, delete, get one/many, shared-audience list & data): 60 requests per minute per channel; plus ≤10 concurrent operations per audienceGroupId on create/add endpoints (429 on excess).…"
  "Set/get webhook endpoint URL: 1,000 requests per minute; Create/delete rich menu & batch-control status: 100 requests per hour (OA-Manager UI actions exempt); Replace/unlink rich menus in batches: 3 requests per hour; Get rich menu list: 10 requests per second.…"
  "Send multicast / membership & coupon endpoints: 200 requests per second; Display loading animation: 100 requests per second; Issue short-lived channel access token: 370 requests per second; ALL OTHER endpoints (incl. GET profile, push, content): 2,000 requests per second.…"
  "Limits use the token-bucket algorithm per endpoint per channel (steady refill, not hourly reset — a fully filled '60/hour' bucket allows e.g. 60 requests in one second before throttling); over-limit requests get HTTP 429; limits apply regardless of IP, and independently per channel even for one OA.…"
  "LINE Login API: no published thresholds; LINE may temporarily restrict bursts of requests (including load testing) if they impact the platform. https://developers.line.biz/en/reference/line-login/ (Rate limits section)"
  "Plan-level monthly quotas (Japan, example): messages counted per RECIPIENT (not per request); sending to blocked/deleted users is not counted; reply messages (and OA-Manager chat/auto-responses) are free; Communication plan ¥0/200 free msgs, Light ¥5,000/5,000, Standard ¥15,000/30,000 + additional up to ¥3/msg.…"
 ]
